# Knowledge Assets

Files in `docs/` are governed Knowledge Assets — containers for meaning, not casual notes.

## Required metadata

Add or update YAML front matter when creating or substantially revising formal assets:

```yaml
---
knowledge_asset_id: ACR-001
title: Human-readable title
classification: Concept Record  # Concept, Decision, Governance, Product, etc.
status: Exploratory             # Exploratory | Draft | Proposed | Approved | Canonical | Superseded | Retired
authority_level: Informational  # Informational | Advisory | Canonical | Governing
owner: John S. Villasenor
last_updated: 2026-07-05
---
```

Seed assets may lack full metadata; add it on the next substantive edit.

## Every asset must answer

- Why it matters
- Who owns it
- Whether it is authoritative
- What decisions it informs
- What context would be lost without it
- How future agents should use it

## Status and promotion

- Do not set **Approved** or **Canonical** without explicit Founder approval
- When superseding an asset, update its status and link the replacement
- Keep exploratory content clearly labeled until promoted

## ID conventions

- `ACR-*` — Architecture/Concept Record
- Match existing prefix patterns in `docs/` for new asset types

Reference: `docs/KNOWLEDGE_ASSET_MODEL.md`
